1
00:00:00,487 --> 00:00:03,314
Fernando, what's this
I've found?

2
00:00:04,309 --> 00:00:06,737
-A cellphone.
-No kidding!

3
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:09,911
I thought it was TV remote.

4
00:00:11,507 --> 00:00:12,984
I know it's a cellphone!

5
00:00:13,391 --> 00:00:15,493
What was it doing
hidden in there?

6
00:00:15,536 --> 00:00:17,615
Is it for talking
to your girlfriends?

7
00:00:17,658 --> 00:00:19,272
-No.
-Are you kidding me?

8
00:00:19,315 --> 00:00:22,295
-No, honey. That's not it.
-It's not?

9
00:00:22,338 --> 00:00:24,718
You probably talk
to your whores on it.

10
00:00:24,761 --> 00:00:27,583
No, I talk to Antonio,
from work, on this phone.

11
00:00:27,626 --> 00:00:32,085
We're on a joint project.
He's on a different provider,

12
00:00:32,128 --> 00:00:33,901
it's cheaper to use this.

13
00:00:33,944 --> 00:00:37,133
I guess Antonio
loves chocolates.

14
00:00:37,513 --> 00:00:40,093
I found the chocolate
next to the phone.

15
00:00:40,136 --> 00:00:43,253
-They were for you!
-You don't say!

16
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:45,598
And this here?

17
00:00:47,097 --> 00:00:48,592
This, what is it?

18
00:00:50,291 --> 00:00:51,663
I talk to Gustavo on it.

19
00:00:52,605 --> 00:00:54,248
Look... Let me guess.

20
00:00:55,118 --> 00:00:57,385
Surely this
is another provider.

21
00:00:57,428 --> 00:00:59,541
Yes, it's another one.

22
00:00:59,584 --> 00:01:01,272
-I'm calling him.
-No.

23
00:01:01,315 --> 00:01:04,447
We were scheduling a match
on Saturday,

24
00:01:04,490 --> 00:01:08,009
but I got disconnected,
I tried to call, didn't work,

25
00:01:08,052 --> 00:01:12,060
and said: "I'll leave the phone
so you can call me".

26
00:01:12,813 --> 00:01:15,831
You know what? Show me
what's in your pockets.

27
00:01:16,689 --> 00:01:20,127
Get up and take everything
out of your pockets. Go on!

28
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:21,791
Yes, here it is.

29
00:01:23,269 --> 00:01:25,587
No, there must be more.

30
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:29,099
These pants have many pockets.
Let's see what you've got.

31
00:01:30,315 --> 00:01:31,369
Look!

32
00:01:32,169 --> 00:01:33,470
Look what I found!

33
00:01:34,068 --> 00:01:35,979
-You organize orgies?
-No.

34
00:01:36,022 --> 00:01:38,490
This is to call my uncle Domingo
in Canada.

35
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:40,031
It's Canadian. Cheaper.

36
00:01:40,074 --> 00:01:43,844
This is for the dentist,
these are old phones.

37
00:01:43,887 --> 00:01:45,225
-You don't say!
-Yes.

38
00:01:45,268 --> 00:01:46,612
I'll have you know

39
00:01:47,491 --> 00:01:48,935
I found more here.

40
00:01:49,905 --> 00:01:50,973
What is this?

41
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:52,776
What is this?

42
00:01:53,366 --> 00:01:54,433
This?

43
00:01:54,873 --> 00:01:55,961
What is it?

44
00:01:56,038 --> 00:01:58,828
On this, you talk
to all your whores, right?

45
00:01:58,871 --> 00:02:02,314
No, these are old phone.
I don't want to dispose of them,

46
00:02:02,357 --> 00:02:04,935
they go into the ocean
and stick into turtles.

47
00:02:04,978 --> 00:02:08,065
I don't want that
on my conscience, Gabriela.

48
00:02:08,108 --> 00:02:09,424
Poor thing!

49
00:02:10,075 --> 00:02:13,776
You have a psychopath, crazy,
insane girlfriend

50
00:02:13,819 --> 00:02:17,179
and you're just trying
to save the turtles.

51
00:02:17,222 --> 00:02:20,005
-I want to save the turtles.
-You're so good!

52
00:02:20,048 --> 00:02:22,241
-Same with batteries.
-Very good.

53
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:26,144
And this? Why lipstick?

54
00:02:28,108 --> 00:02:30,358
-It's chocolate, honey.
-Chocolate?

55
00:02:33,354 --> 00:02:35,522
You're making a fool
of yourself.

56
00:02:41,482 --> 00:02:43,356
Good afternoon.
Your new phone.

57
00:02:43,399 --> 00:02:47,418
Thank you for bringing me
hemorrhoid medicine!